00:48:25,263 --> 00:48:31,263
Teen Wolf is a 1985 American coming-of-age comedy film directed by Rod
Daniel and written by Jeph Loeb and Matthew Weisman.

11
00:53:15,789 --> 00:53:21,789
Fox stars as the title character, a high school student whose ordinary
life is changed when he discovers that he is a werewolf.

12
00:58:06,315 --> 00:58:12,315
James Hampton, Scott Paulin, Susan Ursitti, Jerry Levine, Matt
Adler, and Jay Tarses appear in supporting roles.

13
01:02:56,842 --> 01:03:02,842
Filming took place from November to December 1984.

14
01:07:47,368 --> 01:07:53,368
Teen Wolf was released on August 23, 1985, by Atlantic Releasing
Corporation, and received mixed reviews from film critics.

15
01:12:37,894 --> 01:12:43,894
It was a commercial success, grossing over $33 million domestically on a $4
million budget, with the worldwide gross being over $80 million.

16
01:17:28,421 --> 01:17:34,421
The film's success spawned a titular franchise, including an animated series adaptation in 1986, a sequel film in 1987, the
supernatural live action drama series that aired on MTV from 2011 to 2017, and its continuation film in 2023.

17
01:22:18,947 --> 01:22:24,947
The film explores themes of high school, trainer,
training, coming of age, werewolf.

18
01:27:09,473 --> 01:27:15,473
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
